     1	# AGENT.MD
     2	
     3	This file provides guidance to CodeAgent when working with code in this repository.
     4	
     5	## Overview
     6	
     7	This is CodeAgentPlugin - an extension project that builds on top of OpenCode (agent-kernel) to provide CodeAgent functionality. The repository consists of three main components:
     8	
     9	agent-kernel - Git submodule containing the OpenCode AI coding agent (core kernel)
    10	agent-kernel-extension - Global extensions and built-in plugins that merge into agent-kernel
    11	external-plugins - External plugin system using the @opencode-ai/plugin API
    12	
    13	## 本仓库当前实际状态（2026-11-04 核实）
    14	
    15	以下是当前执行依据；后文逐字保留的原始说明（仅修正 Markdown 格式）包含尚未复刻的目标架构与历史命令，不能据此认定能力已存在或直接执行旧命令。
    16	
    17	- **底座与来源**：原文描述的三层目录在用户最初的仓库中并不存在；已决定以 OpenCode 1.3.17 源码为底座，缺的部分按需复刻补齐。`agent-kernel/` 是只读 submodule，固定在 `517e6c9aa4c61dbc125e7654fc596f1d529f20d9`（`517e6c9aa`，官方 v1.3.17 发布提交）。submodule URL 与本仓库 origin 相同，属于自引用；初始化只用 `git submodule update --init`，**不要用 `--remote`**，不要执行下方历史命令中的远端更新。
    18	- **现有扩展**：`agent-kernel-extension/` 包含 capability-watch、遗留 one-shot worker 两个扩展及 registry，经外置插件公开 loader 的桥接加载。没有原文中的 Init/Server/InternalPlugins/Permission/Tool 五扩展，没有 `kernel/` ACL 层，也没有 GlobalConfig。当前 merge 脚本仅在 `src/custom-hw/`、`src/codeagent/` 下新增带 generated marker 的文件或更新已有同标记文件，不覆盖内核原文件；复制本身不构成 bootstrap。
    19	- **外置与占位目录**：`external-plugins/` 包含 steering 等外置插件；`external-plugins/src/index.ts` 是聚合桥接入口，也是唯一允许 import `agent-kernel-extension` 的外置文件。`sdk/`、`codecov/`、`agents/` 仅占位，不代表原文所述 SDK、Jest mocks 或 agent 能力已经存在。
    20	- **实际可用命令**：测试使用 `node --test …`（完整参数以 `package.json` 的 `test` 脚本为准）；类型检查为 `node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit -p .`；内核边界检查为 `node scripts/check-kernel.mjs`。Bun 1.3.11 在 `~/.bun/bin`。原文中的 Jest、`bun run serve` 和 merge preinstall 尚未复刻，**不要执行**。
    21	- **one-shot 入口**：主流程是 Codex skill `.agents/skills/one-shot/`，设计见 `docs/oneshot/ONE-SHOT-SKILL-DESIGN.md`。`.opencode/skills/one-shot` 与 `agent-kernel-extension/src/codeagent/one-shot` 是遗留的 OpenCode 托管 issue 队列 worker，对应参考流程的“编排层扩展方向”，可选使用。one-shot 不自动合并或发布；PR 与验证证据交由人工评审。
    22	- **硬边界**：不修改 `agent-kernel/` tracked 源码，尤其是 `agent-kernel/packages/` 原文件；不从外置插件 import 内核私有模块。需要内部扩展点时，先证明固定版本确实暴露该入口，否则记录缺口并停止该实现路径。未验证实际 bootstrap，不得声称复制的代码已激活。
    23	- **当前工作流**：编码前写验收标准并核对 v1.3.17 的精确 API；优先在 `external-plugins/` 或项目 skill/command 中做最小实现；运行相关测试与真实 OpenCode smoke test；设计和验证证据保存在 `docs/baseline/`。
    24	
    25	## 编码准则
    26	
    27	请参考如下准则，引自：https://github.com/forrestchang/andrej-karpathy-skills/blob/main/CLAUDE.md?plain=1
    28	
    29	
    30	Behavioral guidelines to reduce common LLM coding mistakes. Merge with project-specific instructions as needed.
    31	
    32	**Tradeoff:** These guidelines bias toward caution over speed. For trivial tasks, use judgment.
    33	
    34	## 1. Think Before Coding
    35	
    36	**Don't assume. Don't hide confusion. Surface tradeoffs.**
    37	
    38	Before implementing:
    39	- State your assumptions explicitly. If uncertain, ask.
    40	- If multiple interpretations exist, present them - don't pick silently.
    41	- If a simpler approach exists, say so. Push back when warranted.
    42	- If something is unclear, stop. Name what's confusing. Ask.
    43	
    44	## 2. Simplicity First
    45	
    46	**Minimum code that solves the problem. Nothing speculative.**
    47	
    48	- No features beyond what was asked.
    49	- No abstractions for single-use code.
    50	- No "flexibility" or "configurability" that wasn't requested.
    51	- No error handling for impossible scenarios.
    52	- If you write 200 lines and it could be 50, rewrite it.
    53	
    54	Ask yourself: "Would a senior engineer say this is overcomplicated?" If yes, simplify.
    55	
    56	## 3. Surgical Changes
    57	
    58	**Touch only what you must. Clean up only your own mess.**
    59	
    60	When editing existing code:
    61	- Don't "improve" adjacent code, comments, or formatting.
    62	- Don't refactor things that aren't broken.
    63	- Match existing style, even if you'd do it differently.
    64	- If you notice unrelated dead code, mention it - don't delete it.
    65	
    66	When your changes create orphans:
    67	- Remove imports/variables/functions that YOUR changes made unused.
    68	- Don't remove pre-existing dead code unless asked.
    69	
    70	The test: Every changed line should trace directly to the user's request.
    71	
    72	## 4. Goal-Driven Execution
    73	
    74	**Define success criteria. Loop until verified.**
    75	
    76	Transform tasks into verifiable goals:
    77	- "Add validation" → "Write tests for invalid inputs, then make them pass"
    78	- "Fix the bug" → "Write a test that reproduces it, then make it pass"
    79	- "Refactor X" → "Ensure tests pass before and after"
    80	
    81	For multi-step tasks, state a brief plan:
    82	[Step] → verify: [check]
    83	[Step] → verify: [check]
    84	[Step] → verify: [check]
    85	
    86	Strong success criteria let you loop independently. Weak criteria ("make it work") require constant clarification.
    87	
    88	---
    89	
    90	**These guidelines are working if:** fewer unnecessary changes in diffs, fewer rewrites due to overcomplication, and clarifying questions come before implementation rather than after mistakes.
    91	
    92	## Development Commands
    93	
    94	```sh
    95	# Initial setup - sync agent-kernel submodule (required before any development)
    96	git submodule sync && git submodule init && git submodule update --remote
    97	
    98	# Install dependencies
    99	bun install                          # root level
   100	cd agent-kernel-extension && bun install   # also runs merge via preinstall
   101	cd external-plugins && bun install
   102	
   103	# Run the server (merges code, then starts opencode)
   104	cd agent-kernel-extension && bun run serve
   105	
   106	# Run tests — two runners exist in this repo (see Testing below)
   107	bun test                                                       # bun:test, from repo root
   108	bun test test/path/to/test.test.ts                             # single test file, from repo root
   109	bun run jtest                                                  # Jest with coverage (see jest.config.ts)
   110	
   111	# Type check
   112	cd external-plugins && bun run typecheck                    # external-plugins (standalone)
   113	cd agent-kernel-extension && bun tsc --noEmit               # extension only (no merge needed)
   114	cd agent-kernel-extension && bun run merge && cd ../agent-kernel && bun run typecheck  # full type check after merge
   115	```
   116	
   117	## Testing
   118	
   119	Test files are *.test.ts in each package's test/ dir, written with bun:test imports. The repo has two runners — know which you are using:
   120	
   121	bun test (root bunfig.toml): canonical for local dev. pathIgnorePatterns skips agent-kernel/** and sdk/js-agentkernel/**; concurrent = false, retry = 3. agent-kernel-extension/bunfig.toml is the per-package config for cd agent-kernel-extension && bun test — when editing coverage/ignore config, update both bunfig files if the change should apply in both contexts.
   122	bun run jtest (jest.config.ts): Jest via ts-jest, used for coverage reporting. Mocks Bun/vitest/@/global via codecov/test/mocks/; @/ resolves to extension or kernel src/. Note: single-file Jest runs can break on the ESM node:path mock — prefer bun test for a single file.
   123	Every test file sets up its own top-of-file mock.module() calls.
   124	
   125	## Architecture
   126	
   127	### Repository Structure
   128	
   129	Top-level: agent-kernel/ (submodule, DO NOT EDIT DIRECTLY), agent-kernel-extension/ (CodeAgent code under src/codeagent/), external-plugins/, codecov/ (Jest-only mocks), sdk/. Use ls for the live tree — src/codeagent/ holds many self-contained subsystems (server, internal-plugins, cron, smart-router, auto-router, checkpoint, turbocontext, sdd, evolve, …) that change often, so don't enumerate them here.
   130	
   131	### Merge Process (merge-agent-kernel.ts)
   132	
   133	agent-kernel-extension/scripts/merge-agent-kernel.ts runs on preinstall/merge/serve. It:
   134	
   135	Merges dependencies external-plugins/package.json → agent-kernel-extension/package.json → agent-kernel/packages/opencode/package.json.
   136	Copies agent-kernel-extension/src/ → agent-kernel/packages/opencode/src/ (CodeAgent code lands in src/codeagent/).
   137	Copies migration scripts → agent-kernel/packages/opencode/migration/, merges script/ → opencode/script/, and merges the js-agentkernel-luban SDK → agent-kernel/packages/sdk/js-agentkernel.
   138	Because the merge overwrites agent-kernel/packages/opencode/src/, never edit merged output there — edit in agent-kernel-extension/src/ and type-check in place (bun tsc --noEmit) or after a merge.
   139	
   140	### Global Extension Entry Points
   141	
   142	Extensions register in agent-kernel/packages/opencode/src/custom-hw/extension/bundled-global-extensions.ts as bundledGlobalExtensions (this path is fixed by the build; do not rename). The array wires, in order: InitExtension, ServerExtension (HTTP routes), InternalPluginsExtension (pushes built-in plugins by priority), PermissionExtension, ToolExtension. Extension points: transformServer / transformInstanceRoutes / transformInternalPlugins / transformPermissionService / transformToolDef.
   143	
   144	## Plugin Implementation Conventions
   145	
   146	### 外置插件优先 (external-first)
   147	
   148	新功能优先在 external-plugins/ 实现（@opencode-ai/plugin Hooks 模式）。外置插件通过 SDK client 与内核交互，不依赖内核内部，内核升级时几乎零成本，且可独立构建发布。
   149	
   150	仅当功能确需 SDK 无法满足的能力时，才用内置插件（agent-kernel-extension/src/codeagent/）：进程内直接调用内核服务、注册全局路由、注册内置 plugin、性能敏感的原生调用。选用内置插件必须在对应设计文档中说明理由（为何 SDK 方案不可行）。外置插件的硬性限制：只能用 SDK client，不能访问 Bus/GlobalBus、Session/SessionStatus 等原生类或任何 agent-kernel 内部 API。
   151	
   152	### 内置插件的内核依赖隔离 (ACL)
   153	
   154	原则：业务代码不直接 @/ import 内核内部（agent-kernel 子模块），一切内核依赖必须经防腐层。内核是易变上游，直接 import 会让每次升级穿透到上百个业务文件；隔离的目的是把升级破坏收口到少数适配器文件。
   155	
   156	每个内置插件模块（src/codeagent/<module>/）自建自己的 kernel/ 防腐层，业务代码只从自己的 <module>/kernel 导入;
   157	
   158	## Key Conventions
   159	
   160	Path aliases (@/, @opencode-ai/sdk/*, @opencode-ai/plugin, test mocks like @/global→mock) are declared in each package's tsconfig.json / package.json — read those for the authoritative list.
   161	Business logic placement: CodeAgent-specific code goes in src/codeagent/ to avoid conflicts with the opencode base.
   162	Configuration: GlobalConfig (src/codeagent/global/config.ts) holds global state; env vars include CODEAGENT_LANGUAGE, CODEAGENT_CURRENT_USER, CODEAGENT_ENV, SCENARIO. External-plugins config loads via loadPluginConfig(); hooks/tools can be disabled via disabled_hooks / disabled_tools.
   163	Style: enforced by Prettier (semi: false, printWidth: 120, root package.json); see AGENTS.md for the full style guide (prefer .catch()/Effect over try/catch, avoid any, single-word var names, early returns over else, const over let).
   164	
   165	## Design Documents
   166	
   167	Design docs live in docs/ (e.g. docs/plugin-guide.md, docs/cron/, docs/auto-router/, docs/baseline/).
   168	Always modify existing design documents rather than creating new ones. Use version numbers in headers (e.g. v4.0), include update date + change log at the end, and follow the existing format.
   169	Per AGENTS.md: after new features, sync docs/baseline/SPEC.md and docs/baseline/DESIGN.md; before a release, review README.md and update CHANGELOG.md.
   170	
   171	## Key Files to Reference
   172	
   173	docs/plugin-guide.md - Complete OpenCode plugin development guide (hooks, events, tools)
   174	agent-kernel-extension/CLAUDE.md - Extension-specific development guide
   175	external-plugins/CLAUDE.md - External plugin development guide with mock module patterns
   176	agent-kernel-extension/src/codeagent/server/index.ts - Main server extension entry
   177	agent-kernel-extension/src/codeagent/internal-plugins/index.ts - Built-in plugins registration
   178	agent-kernel-extension/src/codeagent/kernel/ - Kernel anti-corruption layer (see ACL convention above)
   179	external-plugins/src/index.ts - External plugin entry point
   180	external-plugins/src/hooks/types.ts - Hook type definitions (HookName, InternalHookName)

